    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Système de cote ÉnerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="1" build="19">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.1b19</English>
                <French>v15.1b19</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="11">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.11</English>
                <French>v1.11</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air leakage was the second greatest area of heat loss. Try putting those gaskets under the rest of the ceiling light fixtures and the outlets and light switch plates. An electric damper on the furnace fresh air intake that is wired to the furnace and only opens when the burner is on would reduce that major air leak.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>I added two inches of rigid foam insulation (R-10) to the outside of the walls just to show the difference in heat loss.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>You talked about adding insulation to the attic so I added an extra R-20 to show what difference that would make.</ceilings>
                <foundation>The foundation was the area of greatest heat loss so I finished insulating the floor as an upgrade. </foundation>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
